@SeasonId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@PhaseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Rounds of a season, in the season order (take the id from GET /seasons; defaults: offset 0, limit 25)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/{{SeasonId}}/rounds
Accept: application/json

### Page through the rounds
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/{{SeasonId}}/rounds?offset=0&limit=10
Accept: application/json

### Only the rounds of one phase (take the id from GET /seasons/{id})
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/{{SeasonId}}/rounds?phaseId={{PhaseId}}
Accept: application/json

### Error: the season does not exist (404, unlike GET /rounds?seasonId= which returns an empty list)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/rounds
Accept: application/json

### Error: the season id is not a GUID (404, the route does not match)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/not-a-guid/rounds
Accept: application/json

### Error: limit above the maximum of 100 (400, errors.limit)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/{{SeasonId}}/rounds?limit=1000
Accept: application/json

### Error: negative offset (400, errors.offset)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/seasons/{{SeasonId}}/rounds?offset=-1
Accept: application/json
